# ARROW RIGHT GOES IN, ARROW LEFT COMES OUT (owner, 2026-09-18: "user should be
# able to arrow right into them or to change settings and arrow left out").
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/arrows.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
#
# The rule is not "the arrows are confirm and back". A row that STEPS A VALUE
# answers left and right itself and keeps them -- the gear page turns the figure,
# the title steps the seed, the saves page changes mode. A row that is a DOOR
# answers neither, and only then does the direction mean the door. 90_ui reads
# `UiScreen.handle`'s own answer to tell the two apart, which is why `_on_side`
# had to stop saying yes to every key it was handed.
#
# Proved rather than asserted: the journal below cannot open at all unless right
# opened it, and cannot close unless left closed it.
coast calm
wait 0.6

tap pause
await app:pause 3
wait 0.3
shot 01-home-with-its-rows with app:pause

choose journal
tap move_right
await app:journal 3
wait 0.3
shot 02-right-opened-the-door with app:journal

tap move_left
await app:pause 3
wait 0.3
shot 03-left-came-back-out with app:pause

tap pause
await app:none 3
